  },
  "question": {
    "text": "An unpolarised light beam of intensity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is passed through a polaroid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and then through another polaroid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> which is oriented in such a way that its passing axis makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> relative to that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. The intensity of the emergent light is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>When unpolarized light passes from Polaroid, then it becomes polarised light and intensity becomes half of the original, therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0059_cae8b6f7c5af.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 79px;\" /></p><p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p><p>Using law of&nbsp;Malus&nbsp;for the second polariser,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>We have, intensity of emergent light,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}